---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Authors — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"Who writes and reviews here, and the rule this publication applies to bylines."}
  canonicalPath={"/authors/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .pg-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .pg-head h1 { max-width: 20ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .pg-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }

  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose > * + * { margin-top: 1.375rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 1.15rem + 0.9vw, 1.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.014em; margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 3.25rem); }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .prose p, .prose li { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .prose a:not(.link):not(.btn) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .prose ul.bullets { display: grid; gap: 0.625rem; }
  .prose ul.bullets li {
    padding-left: 1.25rem; position: relative; line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .prose ul.bullets li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.72em;
    inline-size: 5px; block-size: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--line-strong);
  }

  /* Statutory fields that must be filled before launch. Rendered as an
     explicit form-like record rather than invented values — an Impressum
     with made-up details is worse than none. */
  .fields { display: grid; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .fields > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 15rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; padding-block: 0.875rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .fields dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .fields dd { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .fields dd em {
    font-style: normal; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--ember);
    padding-left: 0.75rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--ember-bright);
    display: inline-block; line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .fields > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; } }

  .callout { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem; }
  .callout strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink); }
  .callout--warn { border-left-color: var(--ember-bright); }

  .en-block {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  .en-block h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .en-block p { color: var(--muted); }

  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .listing li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .listing a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.125rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .listing a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .listing h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.012em; }
  .listing p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 60ch; }
  .listing__tail { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .listing a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 17rem) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 9rem); align-items: start; }
    .listing__tail { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.2rem; }
  }

  .sitemap-group { margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .sitemap-group > h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta); font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="pg-head" data-od-id="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/about/">About</a></li>
          <li>Authors</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1>Authors</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every name on this site belongs to a real person who wrote or reviewed the piece it appears on. That rule is why this page is currently short.</p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="band band--tight" data-od-id="authors">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">

        <h2 style="margin-top:0">The byline rule</h2>
        <p>
          Invented authors are among the cheapest ways to make a publication look
          established, and among the fastest ways to destroy its credibility. This site
          does not use them. No article carries a name unless a real person wrote or
          reviewed it, and author pages link to work that can be checked.
        </p>
        <p>
          Until individual author records exist, pieces are credited to the editorial
          desk. That is an accurate description of who is answerable for them, not a
          placeholder standing in for a person.
        </p>

        <h2>Current credits</h2>
      </div>

      <ul class="listing" style="margin-top:1.5rem" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/about/editorial-policy/">
          <h3>Auspicious Music editorial</h3>
          <p>The desk responsible for testing, sourcing and publishing everything currently on the site. Answerable for every technical claim made here.</p>
          <span class="listing__tail">All current articles</span>
        </a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,3.5rem)">
        <h2>What an author page will contain</h2>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Full name, and the areas the person actually works in.</li>
          <li>Verifiable background — released work, credits, or a professional profile that can be checked independently.</li>
          <li>Every article written or reviewed by that person, with the review role stated where it differs from authorship.</li>
          <li>Any commercial relationship that could bear on what they write about.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Reviewers</h2>
        <p>
          Technical pieces may carry a reviewer in addition to an author — someone who
          checked the procedure rather than wrote it up. Where that happens the reviewer
          is named on the article with the date of the review, because a review from three
          years ago says something different about a piece of software than one from last
          month.
        </p>

        <p>
          The standards these credits follow are set out in the
          <a href="/about/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>